# Development configuration template. Copy to config/dev.env (git-ignored)
# and fill in real values; never commit config/dev.env.
#
# aerolink_server.security.load_secret(name, path) reads
# AEROLINK_SECRET_<NAME> from the environment first, falling back to an
# owner-only-permission file at `path` if given. This file documents the
# variable names; it is not sourced automatically by anything.

# Example: a per-node key for local multi-node dev runs. Prefer
# scripts/generate_dev_credentials.py over hand-writing these.
# AEROLINK_SECRET_NODE_1=<64 hex chars, >=32 bytes>
# AEROLINK_SECRET_NODE_2=<64 hex chars, >=32 bytes>

# Where scripts/protocol_coverage.py, scripts/state_explorer.py, and
# scripts/diagnostics_bundle.py write reproducible output; scripts/run_tests.py
# sets this for every case it runs. Left unset, all default to ./artifacts.
# AEROLINK_ARTIFACTS=./artifacts

# server/tools/run_real_sitl.py takes --artifacts and --binary as CLI flags
# instead (see docs/api-examples.md); it does not read environment variables
# for either.
